<title>UK: UK June M4 up final s/a 11.7 % in June.</title>
<headline>UK June M4 up final s/a 11.7 % in June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England published the following data on UK monetary aggregates for June -</p>
<p>   MONEY SUPPLY			June     PVS REPORTED</p>
<p>   M4 in month	 (adjusted)   0.9	    0.9</p>
<p>	in year to date(adjusted)  11.7	   11.6</p>
<p>   M4 in month     (unadjusted)   1.3	    1.2</p>
<p>   in year to date (unadjusted)  11.6	   11.5</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks, building</p>
<p>   societies in billions of stg   5.7	   5.5</p>
<p>The Bank of England said the rise in M4 money supply in the year to June of 11.7 percent was last higher in December 1990 when it was 12.2 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
